[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186184142 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" "question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" "question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" "question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184226 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" "question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" "question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" "question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" "question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" :question/id #uuid "24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-274506" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$\n\nIf $v$ lies in the first quadrant, then $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{36}-\\frac{25}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{36}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6})+(-\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{5}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{55}}{18}-\\frac{10}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{55}-10}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f" :answer/id #uuid "d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{55}-10}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" :question/id #uuid "97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119317" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a-b\\sqrt{1}4}{6},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6}-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-1\\sqrt{14}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,b=1,$ and $a+b=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7b4e39f-b8d2-5d43-9273-97be2dbccbc3" "answer-9975a3bb-76fc-5c77-ae49-5724d89ccc20" "answer-87f86819-67b7-5681-bbb3-b9db74260b7e" "answer-23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f" "answer-13d91780-96a0-5b05-9282-837d0bc5cf2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7b4e39f-b8d2-5d43-9273-97be2dbccbc3" :answer/id #uuid "c7b4e39f-b8d2-5d43-9273-97be2dbccbc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9975a3bb-76fc-5c77-ae49-5724d89ccc20" :answer/id #uuid "9975a3bb-76fc-5c77-ae49-5724d89ccc20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87f86819-67b7-5681-bbb3-b9db74260b7e" :answer/id #uuid "87f86819-67b7-5681-bbb3-b9db74260b7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f" :answer/id #uuid "23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13d91780-96a0-5b05-9282-837d0bc5cf2f" :answer/id #uuid "13d91780-96a0-5b05-9282-837d0bc5cf2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" :question/id #uuid "a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-141359" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\frac{\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b}}{4},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=6,b=2,$ and $a+b=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/id #uuid "d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d409728-f16b-5dbd-989e-4297f678c27d" "answer-bde96f49-8d44-5f49-af06-0fedc038fdc1" "answer-505afb7e-87e3-5258-8fa9-547c7b39ab3f" "answer-4c87b11b-03eb-50d1-a061-8f5cba3a6ef6" "answer-958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d409728-f16b-5dbd-989e-4297f678c27d" :answer/id #uuid "2d409728-f16b-5dbd-989e-4297f678c27d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bde96f49-8d44-5f49-af06-0fedc038fdc1" :answer/id #uuid "bde96f49-8d44-5f49-af06-0fedc038fdc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-505afb7e-87e3-5258-8fa9-547c7b39ab3f" :answer/id #uuid "505afb7e-87e3-5258-8fa9-547c7b39ab3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c87b11b-03eb-50d1-a061-8f5cba3a6ef6" :answer/id #uuid "4c87b11b-03eb-50d1-a061-8f5cba3a6ef6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1" :answer/id #uuid "958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e" :question/id #uuid "dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119320" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v).$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{5}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{5}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7})+(\\frac{2}{3})(-\\frac{2}{7}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{21}-\\frac{4}{21} \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4e4f716-0f36-5041-8ce8-3e1332c0fd72" "answer-cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c" "answer-dc5c049f-d4ae-506d-8359-38c91b104d66" "answer-77a7b2c9-147e-5fc7-9ea6-9c47b3f3c127" "answer-1f0f4507-f336-56f6-86cc-8b6c67aa2f7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4e4f716-0f36-5041-8ce8-3e1332c0fd72" :answer/id #uuid "f4e4f716-0f36-5041-8ce8-3e1332c0fd72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{14}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c" :answer/id #uuid "cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc5c049f-d4ae-506d-8359-38c91b104d66" :answer/id #uuid "dc5c049f-d4ae-506d-8359-38c91b104d66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77a7b2c9-147e-5fc7-9ea6-9c47b3f3c127" :answer/id #uuid "77a7b2c9-147e-5fc7-9ea6-9c47b3f3c127" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f0f4507-f336-56f6-86cc-8b6c67aa2f7b" :answer/id #uuid "1f0f4507-f336-56f6-86cc-8b6c67aa2f7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" :question/id #uuid "4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" :question/math-academy-id "q-141389" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{3}-b\\sqrt{7}}{8},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{4})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4})(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{8}-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}-1\\sqrt{7}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=3,b=1,$ and $a+b=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7d170e4-09b8-54a6-95dc-732e3918ff88" "answer-431f436d-286f-5124-9f57-838cbb663593" "answer-fb6b2054-d008-528a-bf1c-110725aeb7d5" "answer-f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b" "answer-d2d301bb-3dab-58d3-b3c7-a4b5e4f95d3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7d170e4-09b8-54a6-95dc-732e3918ff88" :answer/id #uuid "c7d170e4-09b8-54a6-95dc-732e3918ff88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-431f436d-286f-5124-9f57-838cbb663593" :answer/id #uuid "431f436d-286f-5124-9f57-838cbb663593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb6b2054-d008-528a-bf1c-110725aeb7d5" :answer/id #uuid "fb6b2054-d008-528a-bf1c-110725aeb7d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b" :answer/id #uuid "f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2d301bb-3dab-58d3-b3c7-a4b5e4f95d3e" :answer/id #uuid "d2d301bb-3dab-58d3-b3c7-a4b5e4f95d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" :question/id #uuid "2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" :question/math-academy-id "q-326306" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{5}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{12}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nIf $v$ lies in the second quadrant, then $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, we use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{25}-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{13})(-\\frac{3}{5})+(\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{65}+\\frac{48}{65} \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{65}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749" :answer-field/id #uuid "598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972" :answer/id #uuid "a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{33}{65}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/id #uuid "9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-326383" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{5}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{12}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, then\n\n| $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)$ | $=$ | {{field-1}}$\\,\\,+\\,$ {{field-2}}$\\sqrt{7}$ | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $52$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{16}-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{3}{4})-(\\frac{12}{13})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{52}+\\frac{12\\sqrt{7}}{52} \\\\  & =\\frac{15+12\\sqrt{7}}{52}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd" "answer-field-a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087" :answer/id #uuid "e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0" :answer/id #uuid "2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/id #uuid "f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/math-academy-id "q-144400" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v).$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡u=1-{cos}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡u & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-(-\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{6}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/id #uuid "45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71" "answer-dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" "answer-fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae" "answer-fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c" "answer-8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71" :answer/id #uuid "86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{15}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/id #uuid "dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae" :answer/id #uuid "fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c" :answer/id #uuid "fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6" :answer/id #uuid "8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/id #uuid "bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-326377" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{8}{17},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{15}{17},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, then\n\n| $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)$ | $=$ | {{field-1}}$\\sqrt{3}\\,-\\,$ {{field-2}} | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $34$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{17})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+(\\frac{15}{17})(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{34}-\\frac{15}{34} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}-15}{34}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713" "answer-field-24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d" :answer/id #uuid "3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c" :answer-field/id #uuid "24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5" :answer/id #uuid "df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185347 :tutorial/content "We can compute trigonometric ratios using the sum and difference formulas for sine together with the Pythagorean identity.\n\nLet's suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\sin v = \\dfrac{3}{5}, \\qquad \\cos v = \\dfrac{4}{5}, \\qquad \\sin u = -\\dfrac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nHow can we find the value of $\\sin\\left(u - v\\right)$ given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant? \n\nFirst, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u \\cos v- \\cos u \\sin v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\sin{v}$, $\\cos{v}$, and $\\sin{u}.$ To find the missing value of $\\cos{u}$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 u + \\cos^2 u= 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\cos^2 u = 1- \\sin^2 u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{12}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{12}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{12}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{144}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{144}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\cos u= -\\dfrac{5}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{4}{5})-(-\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{65}+\\frac{15}{65} \\\\  & =-\\frac{33}{65}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184422 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" :question/id #uuid "24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5"] ["question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-274506"] ["question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$\n\nIf $v$ lies in the first quadrant, then $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=${{field-1}}."] ["question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{25}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{36}-\\frac{25}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{11}{36}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6})+(-\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{5}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{55}}{18}-\\frac{10}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{55}-10}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3"] ["answer-d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f" :answer/id #uuid "d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f"] ["answer-d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{55}-10}{18}"] ["answer-field-82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3" :answer-field/correct "answer-d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f"] ["answer-field-82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-d4a6ccf5-14ce-5806-ace1-7ca838a6fd7f"] ["question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-82fa694a-25f2-5e7d-ab30-eca894f443f3"] [17592186184142 :knowledge-point/questions "question-24a538ad-232b-5718-acdd-ce07c94cc6d5"] ["question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" :question/id #uuid "97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e"] ["question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119317"] ["question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a-b\\sqrt{1}4}{6},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$"] ["question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6}-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-1\\sqrt{14}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,b=1,$ and $a+b=3.$"] ["question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6"] ["answer-c7b4e39f-b8d2-5d43-9273-97be2dbccbc3" :answer/id #uuid "c7b4e39f-b8d2-5d43-9273-97be2dbccbc3"] ["answer-c7b4e39f-b8d2-5d43-9273-97be2dbccbc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c7b4e39f-b8d2-5d43-9273-97be2dbccbc3" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-9975a3bb-76fc-5c77-ae49-5724d89ccc20" :answer/id #uuid "9975a3bb-76fc-5c77-ae49-5724d89ccc20"] ["answer-9975a3bb-76fc-5c77-ae49-5724d89ccc20" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9975a3bb-76fc-5c77-ae49-5724d89ccc20" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-87f86819-67b7-5681-bbb3-b9db74260b7e" :answer/id #uuid "87f86819-67b7-5681-bbb3-b9db74260b7e"] ["answer-87f86819-67b7-5681-bbb3-b9db74260b7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-87f86819-67b7-5681-bbb3-b9db74260b7e" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f" :answer/id #uuid "23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f"] ["answer-23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-13d91780-96a0-5b05-9282-837d0bc5cf2f" :answer/id #uuid "13d91780-96a0-5b05-9282-837d0bc5cf2f"] ["answer-13d91780-96a0-5b05-9282-837d0bc5cf2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-13d91780-96a0-5b05-9282-837d0bc5cf2f" :answer/value "9"] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/correct "answer-23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f"] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-c7b4e39f-b8d2-5d43-9273-97be2dbccbc3"] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-9975a3bb-76fc-5c77-ae49-5724d89ccc20"] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-87f86819-67b7-5681-bbb3-b9db74260b7e"] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-23fabac7-34be-5901-889d-cbd6475a113f"] ["answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-13d91780-96a0-5b05-9282-837d0bc5cf2f"] ["question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-826a30ca-938a-5809-9560-1e4fb2a1a3e6"] [17592186184142 :knowledge-point/questions "question-97834400-1835-5bc3-9180-5bacac383a8e"] ["question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" :question/id #uuid "a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8"] ["question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-141359"] ["question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\frac{\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b}}{4},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$"] ["question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=6,b=2,$ and $a+b=8.$"] ["question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/id #uuid "d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93"] ["answer-2d409728-f16b-5dbd-989e-4297f678c27d" :answer/id #uuid "2d409728-f16b-5dbd-989e-4297f678c27d"] ["answer-2d409728-f16b-5dbd-989e-4297f678c27d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2d409728-f16b-5dbd-989e-4297f678c27d" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-bde96f49-8d44-5f49-af06-0fedc038fdc1" :answer/id #uuid "bde96f49-8d44-5f49-af06-0fedc038fdc1"] ["answer-bde96f49-8d44-5f49-af06-0fedc038fdc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bde96f49-8d44-5f49-af06-0fedc038fdc1" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-505afb7e-87e3-5258-8fa9-547c7b39ab3f" :answer/id #uuid "505afb7e-87e3-5258-8fa9-547c7b39ab3f"] ["answer-505afb7e-87e3-5258-8fa9-547c7b39ab3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-505afb7e-87e3-5258-8fa9-547c7b39ab3f" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-4c87b11b-03eb-50d1-a061-8f5cba3a6ef6" :answer/id #uuid "4c87b11b-03eb-50d1-a061-8f5cba3a6ef6"] ["answer-4c87b11b-03eb-50d1-a061-8f5cba3a6ef6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4c87b11b-03eb-50d1-a061-8f5cba3a6ef6" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1" :answer/id #uuid "958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1"] ["answer-958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/correct "answer-958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1"] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/choices "answer-2d409728-f16b-5dbd-989e-4297f678c27d"] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/choices "answer-bde96f49-8d44-5f49-af06-0fedc038fdc1"] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/choices "answer-505afb7e-87e3-5258-8fa9-547c7b39ab3f"] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/choices "answer-4c87b11b-03eb-50d1-a061-8f5cba3a6ef6"] ["answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93" :answer-field/choices "answer-958cbb92-f043-53d1-bb9b-025a90326fd1"] ["question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-d88de4d6-11e4-59ab-b35f-5b9cbf6e3f93"] [17592186184142 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a7374391-644b-5fe8-92d1-774c6f2685b8"] ["question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e" :question/id #uuid "dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e"] ["question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119320"] ["question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v).$"] ["question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{5}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{5}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7})+(\\frac{2}{3})(-\\frac{2}{7}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{21}-\\frac{4}{21} \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00"] ["answer-f4e4f716-0f36-5041-8ce8-3e1332c0fd72" :answer/id #uuid "f4e4f716-0f36-5041-8ce8-3e1332c0fd72"] ["answer-f4e4f716-0f36-5041-8ce8-3e1332c0fd72" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f4e4f716-0f36-5041-8ce8-3e1332c0fd72" :answer/value "-\\frac{14}{21}"] ["answer-cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c" :answer/id #uuid "cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c"] ["answer-cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c" :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{21}"] ["answer-dc5c049f-d4ae-506d-8359-38c91b104d66" :answer/id #uuid "dc5c049f-d4ae-506d-8359-38c91b104d66"] ["answer-dc5c049f-d4ae-506d-8359-38c91b104d66" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dc5c049f-d4ae-506d-8359-38c91b104d66" :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{7}"] ["answer-77a7b2c9-147e-5fc7-9ea6-9c47b3f3c127" :answer/id #uuid "77a7b2c9-147e-5fc7-9ea6-9c47b3f3c127"] ["answer-77a7b2c9-147e-5fc7-9ea6-9c47b3f3c127" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-77a7b2c9-147e-5fc7-9ea6-9c47b3f3c127" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}"] ["answer-1f0f4507-f336-56f6-86cc-8b6c67aa2f7b" :answer/id #uuid "1f0f4507-f336-56f6-86cc-8b6c67aa2f7b"] ["answer-1f0f4507-f336-56f6-86cc-8b6c67aa2f7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1f0f4507-f336-56f6-86cc-8b6c67aa2f7b" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{21}"] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/correct "answer-cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c"] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/choices "answer-f4e4f716-0f36-5041-8ce8-3e1332c0fd72"] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/choices "answer-cf06079f-488c-54c6-9f67-6f54375dcb2c"] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/choices "answer-dc5c049f-d4ae-506d-8359-38c91b104d66"] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/choices "answer-77a7b2c9-147e-5fc7-9ea6-9c47b3f3c127"] ["answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00" :answer-field/choices "answer-1f0f4507-f336-56f6-86cc-8b6c67aa2f7b"] ["question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3b2f076d-ce9b-57f9-98c4-9fb84d87fd00"] [17592186184142 :knowledge-point/questions "question-dbced5cb-cb8f-554f-bc5c-eb4739e6f20e"] ["question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" :question/id #uuid "4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57"] ["question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" :question/math-academy-id "q-141389"] ["question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a\\sqrt{3}-b\\sqrt{7}}{8},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$"] ["question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡v=1-{sin}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡v & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{4})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4})(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{8}-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}-1\\sqrt{7}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=3,b=1,$ and $a+b=4.$"] ["question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9"] ["answer-c7d170e4-09b8-54a6-95dc-732e3918ff88" :answer/id #uuid "c7d170e4-09b8-54a6-95dc-732e3918ff88"] ["answer-c7d170e4-09b8-54a6-95dc-732e3918ff88" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c7d170e4-09b8-54a6-95dc-732e3918ff88" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-431f436d-286f-5124-9f57-838cbb663593" :answer/id #uuid "431f436d-286f-5124-9f57-838cbb663593"] ["answer-431f436d-286f-5124-9f57-838cbb663593" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-431f436d-286f-5124-9f57-838cbb663593" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-fb6b2054-d008-528a-bf1c-110725aeb7d5" :answer/id #uuid "fb6b2054-d008-528a-bf1c-110725aeb7d5"] ["answer-fb6b2054-d008-528a-bf1c-110725aeb7d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fb6b2054-d008-528a-bf1c-110725aeb7d5" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b" :answer/id #uuid "f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b"] ["answer-f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-d2d301bb-3dab-58d3-b3c7-a4b5e4f95d3e" :answer/id #uuid "d2d301bb-3dab-58d3-b3c7-a4b5e4f95d3e"] ["answer-d2d301bb-3dab-58d3-b3c7-a4b5e4f95d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d2d301bb-3dab-58d3-b3c7-a4b5e4f95d3e" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/correct "answer-f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b"] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/choices "answer-c7d170e4-09b8-54a6-95dc-732e3918ff88"] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/choices "answer-431f436d-286f-5124-9f57-838cbb663593"] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/choices "answer-fb6b2054-d008-528a-bf1c-110725aeb7d5"] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/choices "answer-f71b7119-0fb5-5212-83f2-49afd258fc8b"] ["answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9" :answer-field/choices "answer-d2d301bb-3dab-58d3-b3c7-a4b5e4f95d3e"] ["question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5b2abad3-93fb-5e4a-a512-cc96b4e71bd9"] [17592186184226 :knowledge-point/questions "question-4643f6f8-6def-57fc-9f05-9106c1781f57"] ["question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" :question/id #uuid "2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71"] ["question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" :question/math-academy-id "q-326306"] ["question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{5}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{12}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nIf $v$ lies in the second quadrant, then $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=${{field-1}}."] ["question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, we use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{25}-\\frac{9}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the second quadrant, where sine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{13})(-\\frac{3}{5})+(\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{65}+\\frac{48}{65} \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{65}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749" :answer-field/id #uuid "598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749"] ["answer-a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972" :answer/id #uuid "a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972"] ["answer-a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972" :answer/value "\\frac{33}{65}"] ["answer-field-598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749" :answer-field/correct "answer-a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972"] ["answer-field-598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749" :answer-field/choices "answer-a9ff4504-ac7a-57d3-a336-b4500ec61972"] ["question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-598d1261-b549-515b-a77a-1a37d5829749"] [17592186184226 :knowledge-point/questions "question-2e61a3ba-7f7b-576c-9651-31afc3ef6f71"] ["question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/id #uuid "9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0"] ["question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-326383"] ["question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{5}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{12}{13},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, then\n\n| $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)$ | $=$ | {{field-1}}$\\,\\,+\\,$ {{field-2}}$\\sqrt{7}$ | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $52$ |  |"] ["question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{16}-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{3}{4})-(\\frac{12}{13})(-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{52}+\\frac{12\\sqrt{7}}{52} \\\\  & =\\frac{15+12\\sqrt{7}}{52}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd"] ["answer-e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087" :answer/id #uuid "e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087"] ["answer-e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087" :answer/value "15"] ["answer-field-ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd" :answer-field/correct "answer-e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087"] ["answer-field-ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd" :answer-field/choices "answer-e1710ed1-4caf-58bf-82be-5d414220e087"] ["answer-field-a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05"] ["answer-2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0" :answer/id #uuid "2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0"] ["answer-2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0" :answer/value "12"] ["answer-field-a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05" :answer-field/correct "answer-2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0"] ["answer-field-a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05" :answer-field/choices "answer-2a040c0f-a1fd-58ed-aad2-fe5b5cf047d0"] ["question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ed949f4a-0931-51ac-8da5-094e551428fd"] ["question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a7103d3e-80a2-5de4-ac0e-a10a2142cb05"] [17592186184226 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9ecd9133-5002-52de-bbff-55ef2618e8b0"] ["question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/id #uuid "f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06"] ["question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/math-academy-id "q-144400"] ["question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v).$"] ["question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡u=1-{cos}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡u & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-(-\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{6}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/id #uuid "45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2"] ["answer-86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71" :answer/id #uuid "86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71"] ["answer-86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71" :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{15}}{6}"] ["answer-dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/id #uuid "dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3"] ["answer-dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}"] ["answer-fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae" :answer/id #uuid "fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae"] ["answer-fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae" :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{5}}{6}"] ["answer-fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c" :answer/id #uuid "fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c"] ["answer-fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c" :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{6}"] ["answer-8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6" :answer/id #uuid "8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6"] ["answer-8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{5}}{6}"] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/correct "answer-dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3"] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/choices "answer-86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71"] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/choices "answer-dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3"] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/choices "answer-fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae"] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/choices "answer-fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c"] ["answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/choices "answer-8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6"] ["question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2"] [17592186184226 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06"] ["question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/id #uuid "bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f"] ["question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-326377"] ["question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{8}{17},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{15}{17},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, then\n\n| $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)$ | $=$ | {{field-1}}$\\sqrt{3}\\,-\\,$ {{field-2}} | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $34$ |  |"] ["question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,$ we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡v=1-{cos}^{2}⁡v\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡v & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡v \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $v$ lies in the fourth quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{17})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+(\\frac{15}{17})(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{34}-\\frac{15}{34} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}-15}{34}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713"] ["answer-3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d" :answer/id #uuid "3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d"] ["answer-3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-field-ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713" :answer-field/correct "answer-3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d"] ["answer-field-ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713" :answer-field/choices "answer-3fa37d87-2d10-5b67-a6d0-78d0e0a5a54d"] ["answer-field-24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c" :answer-field/id #uuid "24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c"] ["answer-df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5" :answer/id #uuid "df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5"] ["answer-df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5" :answer/value "15"] ["answer-field-24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c" :answer-field/correct "answer-df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5"] ["answer-field-24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c" :answer-field/choices "answer-df83a4e1-66ba-5873-97da-2d74aacdb5f5"] ["question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ab314b19-c35e-5b2b-9cf9-5dbd3ed37713"] ["question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-24922baa-2702-5f4a-9cd9-809ee303d03c"] [17592186184226 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bb1f9724-9227-5181-ae8d-25a299447d4f"] [17592186185347 :tutorial/content "We can compute trigonometric ratios using the sum and difference formulas for sine together with the Pythagorean identity.\n\nLet's suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\sin v = \\dfrac{3}{5}, \\qquad \\cos v = \\dfrac{4}{5}, \\qquad \\sin u = -\\dfrac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nHow can we find the value of $\\sin\\left(u - v\\right)$ given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant? \n\nFirst, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u \\cos v- \\cos u \\sin v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\sin{v}$, $\\cos{v}$, and $\\sin{u}.$ To find the missing value of $\\cos{u}$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 u + \\cos^2 u= 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\cos^2 u = 1- \\sin^2 u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{12}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{12}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{12}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{144}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{144}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\cos u= -\\dfrac{5}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{4}{5})-(-\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{65}+\\frac{15}{65} \\\\  & =-\\frac{33}{65}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186184422 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0]] "retractions" [[17592186185347 :tutorial/content "We can compute trigonometric ratios using the sum and difference formulas for sine together with the Pythagorean identity.\n\nLet's suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\sin v = \\dfrac{3}{5}, \\qquad \\cos v = \\dfrac{4}{5}, \\qquad \\sin u = -\\dfrac{12}{13}.\n$$\n\nHow can we find the value of $\\sin\\left(u - v\\right)$ given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant? \n\nFirst, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u \\cos v- \\cos u \\sin v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\sin{v}$, $\\cos{v}$, and $\\sin{u}.$ To find the missing value of $\\cos{u}$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 u + \\cos^2 u= 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\cos^2 u = 1- \\sin^2 u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}u & =1-{sin}^{2}u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{12}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{12}{13})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{12}^{2}}{{13}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{144}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{169}{169}-\\frac{144}{169} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{169}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{169}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where cosine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\cos u= -\\dfrac{5}{13}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}u\\operatorname{cos}v-\\operatorname{cos}u\\operatorname{sin}v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{12}{13})(\\frac{4}{5})-(-\\frac{5}{13})(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{65}+\\frac{15}{65} \\\\  & =-\\frac{33}{65}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"]]}]